                                                "sense_id": "959acca2-267d-3984-a2a1-3d610fa168a0",
                                                "text": "Others within the Cartesian tradition took the idea of a light-bearing medium in quite different directions. For instance, in 1690 Christiaan Huygens considered light to be a sequence of pulses traveling at a finite velocity within the medium."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
